stop [SimTalk] - EventController
Stops the EventController designated by <Path> and thus terminates the simulation run.
Remarks
The simulation will not stop until the current method execution (including the entire call stack) finished or
was suspended. A wait-statement will for example suspend method execution.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.stop([EndSim:boolean:=false])
Parameter
The optional parameter EndSim of data type boolean set if the simulation will be stopped and if the
endSim methods will be executed (true) or if the simulation will only be stopped (false).
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Example
root.EventController.stop
SimTalk
endSim [SimTalk]
See also
Start/Stop Simulation [EventController]
wait [SimTalk]
Suspending Methods
